Here are two polished versions tailored for different contexts, both preserving all original technical details while improving flow, vocabulary, and readability.

### Option 1: Fluent Technical Prose (Best for papers, abstracts, or descriptions)
> "A semiconductor device is provided that enhances overall performance by enabling variable adjustment of the threshold voltage in a gate-all-around (GAA) transistor structure. The device includes a substrate comprising a first region and a second region. Disposed above and spaced apart from the substrate are a first wire pattern on the first region and a second wire pattern on the second region. First and second gate insulating films envelop the perimeters of the first and second wire patterns, respectively. Positioned on the first gate insulating film and intersecting the first wire pattern, a first gate electrode incorporates a first metal oxide film. A second gate electrode is positioned on the second gate insulating film and intersects the second wire pattern. Additionally, first and second gate spacers are disposed on the sidewalls of the first and second gate electrodes, respectively."

### Option 2: Formal Patent/Claim Style (Best for legal or formal technical documentation)
> "Provided herein is a semiconductor device configured to enhance performance by variably adjusting the threshold voltage of a gate-all-around transistor structure. The semiconductor device comprises:
> * a substrate having a first region and a second region;
> * a first wire pattern disposed on the first region and spaced apart from the substrate;
> * a second wire pattern disposed on the second region and spaced apart from the substrate;
> * a first gate insulating film surrounding a perimeter of the first wire pattern;
> * a second gate insulating film surrounding a perimeter of the second wire pattern;
> * a first gate electrode disposed on the first gate insulating film, intersecting the first wire pattern, and incorporating a first metal oxide film therein;
> * a second gate electrode disposed on the second gate insulating film and intersecting the second wire pattern;
> * a first gate spacer positioned on a sidewall of the first gate electrode; and
> * a second gate spacer positioned on a sidewall of the second gate electrode."

### Key Improvements Made:
* **Enhanced Vocabulary:** Replaced repetitive phrases like *"provided on"* and *"surrounding a perimeter of"* with varied, precise technical terms (*"disposed on," "positioned on," "envelops"*).
* **Improved Sentence Flow:** Smoothed out the clunky opening (*"There is provided..."*) and restructured repetitive parallel clauses into a cohesive narrative.
* **Maintained 100% Accuracy:** Preserved all functional relationships, regions, and structural components without omitting or altering any details.
